/* Airline Agent Policy — tau2-airline (variant-set run1)

   Translated from experiments/translation/spec.md against the live
   traces captured in outputs/variant-set/run1/ (95 oracle-labeled
   decision points, 397 nodes, 2550 edges) and the trace-derived
   system profile in outputs/variant-set/run1/system.md.

   Enforcement target: the airline customer-service assistant, which
   the instrumentation records under msg.agent = "LLMAgent". Content
   checks use the custom C++ functors declared below and implemented
   in airline_functors.cpp (keyword/phrase matchers, not
   @llm_check_fn — no LLM oracle is assumed).

   Round-trip audit: PASS (2026-08-19) — the rules were read back
   without the English spec and reconstructed clause by clause. That
   pass found four encoding gaps (C11 fired on a call naming no
   flights, C16 excluded travel certificates instead of requiring a
   gift or credit card, C13 named its tool class by exception, and
   the C20 parse-failure guard was unexplained) and one uncovered
   spec sentence (bags the user never asked for, now C27). All five
   are fixed; the reconstruction now matches the spec.
*/
#include "../../../../policies/common_policy.dl"

/* ── K-Constraints (verified against the captured traces) ──────────

   K1: The end user's turns are recorded as msg.agent = "LLMAgent"
       AND msg.agent_role = $UserRole() (333 nodes). The SAME user
       text also appears as (agent="UserSimulator", role=Assistant),
       and the ASSISTANT's own replies appear as
       (agent="UserSimulator", role=$UserRole()) — 333 nodes each.
       A rule keyed on $UserRole() alone therefore reads the agent's
       own words back as if the user had said them. Every rule that
       reads user content in this policy filters on BOTH fields.
       Evidence: system.md "Role collisions"; scenario 79's slice
       carries both mirrors of every turn.

   K2: Tool results are (agent="LLMAgent", role=$AgentType()) nodes
       whose msg.contents is the raw tool payload; the same node
       carries ToolResult(id, fn_name, args) (369 nodes). Tool
       results are read through msg.contents, never through
       ToolResult's args.

   K3: get_user_details returns a JSON object with a bare string
       field "membership" (regular|silver|gold) and a
       "payment_methods" OBJECT keyed by payment id
       (credit_card_*, gift_card_*, certificate_*).

   K4: get_reservation_details, cancel_reservation, book_reservation
       and the three update_reservation_* tools all return the same
       JSON reservation object: reservation_id, user_id, origin,
       destination, flight_type, cabin, created_at, insurance,
       total_baggages, nonfree_baggages, flights[] (flight_number,
       origin, destination, date, status), passengers[] (first_name,
       last_name, dob), payment_history[].

   K5: search_direct_flight returns a JSON ARRAY and
       search_onestop_flight an ARRAY OF ARRAYS, so a top-level
       @json_get_str on them returns "" (system.md warnings). Flight
       lookups therefore go through @flight_known / @flight_serves,
       which scan for flight objects at any depth. get_flight_status
       returns a BARE STRING ("landed"), not JSON, and calculate
       returns a bare number — neither is read with a JSON accessor.

   K6: A tool call denied by policy is recorded WITHOUT a ToolResult
       fact (packages/sasy/sasy/instrumentation/tau2.py records the
       denial event with no derived_from), while a call that ran —
       even one that returned "Error: ..." — does carry one. So
       ToolResult(_, fn, args) proves that exact call was authorized
       and executed, which is what makes the retry exemption in C4
       safe: a blocked call cannot bootstrap itself.

   K7: Every current node carries the agent's whole linear history as
       EdgeData(src, current, [proximal, message_index]) with
       message_index >= 0 (95/95 slices; 0 slices lack an indexed
       user turn). The most recent user turn is the indexed user turn
       with the largest message_index.

   K8: Decision points batch parallel tool calls — 39 of 95 current
       nodes propose 2 to 6 calls, and the oracle authorizes the
       parallel reads. The spec's "one tool call at a time" sentence
       is therefore NOT enforced as a denial (see "Not enforced").

   K9: Captured decision points carry no roles
       (provenance.roles_unknown), and the tau2 deployment
       authenticates one service identity for every conversation. No
       clause is gated on HasRole; authorization is by tool plus
       conversation state.

   K10: transfer_to_human_agents was called 4 times and produced no
       result node (system.md warnings), so no rule may join on a
       ToolResult for it.

   K11: The deployment checks tool calls only — sasy's tau2
       instrumentation has no SendAttempt/message hook — so message
       actions are out of scope for this policy.

   K12: The domain runs on a fixed clock: the spec states the current
       time as 2024-05-15 15:00:00 EST, and the captured reservations
       are dated around it. The two rules that need "now" (the
       24-hour cancellation window in C20 and the flown-segment test
       behind C12/C19) carry that timestamp as a literal. On a
       deployment with a moving clock both literals have to be
       replaced with the real current time.
   ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

/* ── Structured Spec ───────────────────────────────────────────────

   C1:  Allow the airline agent's read/informational tools
        (get_user_details, get_reservation_details,
        search_direct_flight, search_onestop_flight,
        get_flight_status, calculate, think) — they do not touch the
        booking database.
   C2:  Allow the write tools (book/cancel/update_*, send_certificate)
        and transfer_to_human_agents, subject to C4-C25; deny any tool
        outside the airline toolset.
   C3:  A request that violates this policy is refused with an error
        (deny, not passthrough).
   C4:  Deny a booking-database write (book_reservation,
        cancel_reservation, update_reservation_flights /
        _baggages / _passengers) unless the most recent user turn
        gives an explicit go-ahead, or the identical call was already
        authorized and executed earlier in this conversation.
   C5:  Deny book_reservation unless the user id was obtained — a
        get_user_details result for that user_id is in the chain.
   C6:  Deny book_reservation with more than five passengers.
   C7:  Deny book_reservation using more than one travel certificate,
        more than one credit card, or more than three gift cards.
   C8:  Deny a payment-bearing call that uses a payment method absent
        from the user's profile, when the profile is in the chain.
   C9:  Deny a write to a reservation whose details were never
        retrieved (no get_reservation_details result for that
        reservation id), and deny one that names no reservation id:
        the API does not check the rules for the agent.
   C10: Deny update_reservation_flights that changes the flights of a
        basic-economy reservation (a cabin-only change is allowed).
   C11: Deny update_reservation_flights whose new itinerary provably
        no longer serves the reservation's origin or destination.
   C12: Deny a cabin change when any flight in the reservation has
        already been flown.
   C13: Deny update_reservation_baggages that reduces the checked-bag
        count, or that charges for more bags than the reservation
        carries.
   C14: Deny update_reservation_passengers that changes the NUMBER of
        passengers.
   C15: Deny update_reservation_passengers that substitutes the
        travellers outright (no passenger keeps a surname or a date of
        birth).
   C16: Deny paying for a flight change with a travel certificate —
        the spec allows a single gift card or credit card.
   C17: Deny cancel_reservation when the reservation's owner has not
        been established (no profile lookup for that user id and no
        user turn stating it).
   C18: Deny cancel_reservation when the user never stated a reason
        for cancelling.
   C19: Deny cancel_reservation when any portion of the trip has
        already been flown — that case needs a human agent.
   C20: Deny cancel_reservation unless one of the four grounds holds:
        booked within the last 24 hours, the airline cancelled a
        flight, the cabin is business, or the reservation has travel
        insurance and the stated reason is covered.
   C21: Deny send_certificate unless the user explicitly asked for
        compensation — no proactive offers.
   C22: Deny send_certificate to a regular member.
   C23: Deny send_certificate when the membership level was never
        verified, or when the call names no user.
   C24: Deny send_certificate unless a cancelled or delayed flight is
        confirmed on a reservation belonging to that user.
   C25: Deny send_certificate whose amount is not $100 per passenger
        (cancelled flight) or $50 per passenger (delayed flight).
   C26: Allow transfer_to_human_agents — escalation is how the agent
        handles what it may not do itself.
   C27: Deny a call that puts checked bags on a reservation when the
        user never asked for any.

   Not enforced, and why:

   * "Only one tool call at a time, and never a message alongside a
     tool call" — K8: parallel reads are the norm in the traces and
     the oracle authorizes them. Enforcing it would deny 30+ labeled
     decision points that are otherwise correct.
   * "List the action details" — C4 enforces the second half of that
     sentence, the user's explicit confirmation, and not the first.
     What the agent said before the user answered is a message, and
     judging whether a message "lists the action details" is a
     semantic test this policy has no deterministic form of. In
     practice the confirmation carries it: a user does not say "yes,
     go ahead" to a plan they were never shown.
   * "Do not provide information or procedures outside the tools, and
     no subjective recommendations" — K11: this constrains message
     text, and the deployment submits no message actions for checking.
   * "Cabin class must be the same across all flights" — the API takes
     one cabin per reservation, so a per-flight mismatch cannot be
     expressed in a call.
   * "The user cannot add insurance after initial booking" — no
     update_reservation_* tool takes an insurance argument
     (benchmarks/tau2-airline/tools.json), so the call does not exist.
   * The free-checked-bag allowance table (0-4 bags by cabin and
     membership) — the traces contain oracle-authorized calls that
     over-charge the user against this table (a gold member charged
     for 3 bags in economy), so encoding it as a denial would reject
     labeled-correct behaviour. The narrower invariant that survives,
     "never charge for more bags than the reservation carries", is
     enforced in C13.
   * "Trip type must not change" — the update call takes no
     flight_type argument and the leg count is not a reliable proxy
     for it (a round trip can have two legs or four).
   ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   CUSTOM C++ FUNCTORS (airline_functors.cpp)
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* Content classifiers over user message text. */
.functor user_confirms_action(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor user_states_cancel_reason(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor covered_cancel_reason(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor user_requests_compensation(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor user_mentions_bags(text: symbol): unsigned stateful

/* JSON structure helpers over call arguments and tool payloads. */
.functor flights_same(args: symbol, res: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor passengers_substituted(args: symbol, res: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor any_flight_flown(res: symbol, cutoff: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor res_flight_status_present(res: symbol, status: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor payment_missing_from_profile(args: symbol, profile: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor count_payment_prefix(args: symbol, prefix: symbol): number stateful
.functor flight_known(haystack: symbol, fnum: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor flight_serves(haystack: symbol, fnum: symbol, airport: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor json_len(json: symbol, field: symbol): number stateful

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   TOOL CLASSES
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* Every tool the airline agent is allowed to call (C1, C2, C26). */
.decl AirlineTool(fn: symbol)
AirlineTool("book_reservation").
AirlineTool("cancel_reservation").
AirlineTool("update_reservation_flights").
AirlineTool("update_reservation_baggages").
AirlineTool("update_reservation_passengers").
AirlineTool("send_certificate").
AirlineTool("transfer_to_human_agents").
AirlineTool("get_reservation_details").
AirlineTool("get_user_details").
AirlineTool("get_flight_status").
AirlineTool("search_direct_flight").
AirlineTool("search_onestop_flight").
AirlineTool("calculate").
AirlineTool("think").

/* Writes that address an existing reservation by id. */
.decl ReservationWriteTool(fn: symbol)
ReservationWriteTool("cancel_reservation").
ReservationWriteTool("update_reservation_flights").
ReservationWriteTool("update_reservation_baggages").
ReservationWriteTool("update_reservation_passengers").

/* Everything that updates the booking database (C4). */
.decl BookingDbWriteTool(fn: symbol)
BookingDbWriteTool("book_reservation").
BookingDbWriteTool(fn) :- ReservationWriteTool(fn).

/* Calls that carry checked-bag counts (C13, C27). */
.decl BaggageBearingTool(fn: symbol)
BaggageBearingTool("book_reservation").
BaggageBearingTool("update_reservation_baggages").

/* Calls that move money and therefore name a payment method (C8). */
.decl PaymentBearingTool(fn: symbol)
PaymentBearingTool("book_reservation").
PaymentBearingTool("update_reservation_flights").
PaymentBearingTool("update_reservation_baggages").

/* Tools whose result payload is a reservation object (K4). */
.decl ReservationReturningTool(fn: symbol)
ReservationReturningTool("get_reservation_details").
ReservationReturningTool("cancel_reservation").
ReservationReturningTool("book_reservation").
ReservationReturningTool("update_reservation_flights").
ReservationReturningTool("update_reservation_baggages").
ReservationReturningTool("update_reservation_passengers").

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   GRAPH TRAVERSAL GATE

   Only the write tools consult conversation history; the read tools
   are authorized on the tool name alone. Gating CurrentDepends on
   them keeps the backward traversal out of the hot path for the
   read-heavy majority of decision points (73 of the 95 captured
   ones).
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :- IsTool(_, "book_reservation").
CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :- IsTool(_, "cancel_reservation").
CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :- IsTool(_, "update_reservation_flights").
CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :- IsTool(_, "update_reservation_baggages").
CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :- IsTool(_, "update_reservation_passengers").
CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :- IsTool(_, "send_certificate").

/* No rule in this policy consumes ReachableFrom — the pairwise
   forward-reachability relation — so its gate is deliberately left
   unsatisfiable. Declaring a rule for it at all is what matters:
   sugar.py emits a trivially-true default only for gates the policy
   declares no rule for, and it decides "this policy uses
   ReachableFrom" by scanning text that, through this include path,
   still carries common_policy's own rules. Without this line the
   default fires and the quadratic relation is built on every write
   decision for nothing. The body names a tool this domain does not
   have, so the head never holds. */
ReachableFromPolicyRelevant() :- IsTool(_, "__no_tool_uses_reachable_from__").

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   CONVERSATION STATE

   Everything below reads the backward slice of the current action.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* K1: a turn the END USER addressed to the airline agent. Both
   filters are load-bearing — the same text is mirrored under
   agent = "UserSimulator", and that mirror also carries the agent's
   own replies with role = $UserRole(). */
.decl UserTurn(id: symbol)
UserTurn(id) :-
    CurrentDepends(id),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    msg.agent = "LLMAgent",
    msg.agent_role = $UserRole().

/* K7: user turns positioned in the agent's linear history. */
.decl IndexedUserTurn(pos: number, id: symbol)
IndexedUserTurn(pos, id) :-
    Current(cur),
    EdgeData(id, cur, ed),
    pos = ed.message_index,
    pos >= 0,
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    msg.agent = "LLMAgent",
    msg.agent_role = $UserRole().

/* The turn the agent is acting on: the most recent user turn. */
.decl LatestUserTurn(id: symbol)
LatestUserTurn(id) :-
    IndexedUserTurn(pos, id),
    pos = max q : { IndexedUserTurn(q, _) }.

/* K2/K4: reservation payloads seen in this conversation, keyed by
   reservation id. Failed writes return a bare "Error: ..." string,
   which yields no reservation_id and so contributes nothing. */
.decl ReservationPayload(rid: symbol, body: symbol)
ReservationPayload(rid, body) :-
    CurrentDepends(mid),
    ToolResult(mid, fn, _),
    ReservationReturningTool(fn),
    SentMessage(mid, msg),
    body = msg.contents,
    rid = @json_get_str(body, "reservation_id"),
    rid != "".

/* C9: the domain's declared lookup tool actually ran for this
   reservation (benchmarks/tau2-airline/tools.json names
   get_reservation_details as the lookup tool). */
.decl ReservationLookedUp(rid: symbol)
ReservationLookedUp(rid) :-
    CurrentDepends(mid),
    ToolResult(mid, "get_reservation_details", _),
    SentMessage(mid, msg),
    rid = @json_get_str(msg.contents, "reservation_id"),
    rid != "".

/* Reservation attributes. Several payloads may describe the same
   reservation (a lookup, then the result of a write), so the rules
   below treat these as evidence rather than as a single truth. */
.decl ResUser(rid: symbol, uid: symbol)
ResUser(rid, uid) :-
    ReservationPayload(rid, body),
    uid = @json_get_str(body, "user_id"),
    uid != "".

.decl ResCabin(rid: symbol, cabin: symbol)
ResCabin(rid, cabin) :-
    ReservationPayload(rid, body),
    cabin = @json_get_str(body, "cabin"),
    cabin != "".

.decl ResInsurance(rid: symbol, ins: symbol)
ResInsurance(rid, ins) :-
    ReservationPayload(rid, body),
    ins = @json_get_str(body, "insurance"),
    ins != "".

.decl ResCreated(rid: symbol, ts: symbol)
ResCreated(rid, ts) :-
    ReservationPayload(rid, body),
    ts = @json_get_str(body, "created_at"),
    ts != "".

.decl ResBags(rid: symbol, n: number)
ResBags(rid, n) :-
    ReservationPayload(rid, body),
    n = @json_get_int(body, "total_baggages").

.decl ResPassengerCount(rid: symbol, n: number)
ResPassengerCount(rid, n) :-
    ReservationPayload(rid, body),
    n = @json_len(body, "passengers"),
    n > 0.

/* The two airports the trip must keep serving (C11). */
.decl ResEndpoint(rid: symbol, airport: symbol)
ResEndpoint(rid, ap) :-
    ReservationPayload(rid, body),
    ap = @json_get_str(body, "origin"),
    ap != "".
ResEndpoint(rid, ap) :-
    ReservationPayload(rid, body),
    ap = @json_get_str(body, "destination"),
    ap != "".

/* K3: verified membership level, scoped to the profile's own user
   id rather than to whichever profile happens to be in the chain. */
.decl UserProfile(uid: symbol, body: symbol)
UserProfile(uid, body) :-
    CurrentDepends(mid),
    ToolResult(mid, "get_user_details", _),
    SentMessage(mid, msg),
    body = msg.contents,
    uid = @json_get_str(body, "user_id"),
    uid != "".

.decl MembershipOf(uid: symbol, level: symbol)
MembershipOf(uid, level) :-
    UserProfile(uid, body),
    level = @json_get_str(body, "membership"),
    level != "".

/* Any tool payload in the chain — the haystack flight lookups scan
   (K5: reservations, direct-flight arrays, one-stop arrays). */
.decl ChainPayload(body: symbol)
ChainPayload(body) :-
    CurrentDepends(mid),
    ToolResult(mid, _, _),
    SentMessage(mid, msg),
    body = msg.contents,
    body != "".

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   THE ACTION UNDER EVALUATION
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* The reservation a write addresses. */
.decl ActionRes(idx: unsigned, rid: symbol)
ActionRes(idx, rid) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    a = $CallTool(fn, args),
    ReservationWriteTool(fn),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    rid != "".

/* The user a call is on behalf of: named directly by
   book_reservation and send_certificate, and taken from the
   reservation for the update/cancel tools. */
.decl ActionUser(idx: unsigned, uid: symbol)
ActionUser(idx, uid) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    a = $CallTool(fn, args),
    BookingDbWriteTool(fn),
    uid = @json_get_str(args, "user_id"),
    uid != "".
ActionUser(idx, uid) :-
    ActionRes(idx, rid),
    ResUser(rid, uid).

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   C1/C2/C3: BASE AUTHORIZATION
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* C1, C2: the airline toolset is allowed; the deny rules below
   carve out the cases the policy forbids. */
IsAuthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    a = $CallTool(fn, _),
    AirlineTool(fn).

/* C3: a refused call comes back as an error the agent can relay,
   not as a silent passthrough. */
DenyUnauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsToolCall(a).

/* C2: nothing outside the airline toolset. */
// @deny_message: This tool is not part of the airline agent's toolset.
// @suggestion: Use the airline tools (search, get_*, book, update_*, cancel, send_certificate, transfer_to_human_agents) or transfer the user to a human agent.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    a = $CallTool(fn, _),
    !AirlineTool(fn).

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   C4: EXPLICIT USER CONFIRMATION BEFORE ANY DATABASE WRITE
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* The user's latest turn hands the action over ("yes, please go
   ahead", "please proceed with this change"). A bare "yes" attached
   to a preference ("Yes, I want to keep Economy") is not a
   confirmation — see airline_functors.cpp. */
.decl UserConfirmedLatestTurn()
UserConfirmedLatestTurn() :-
    LatestUserTurn(id),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    @user_confirms_action(msg.contents) = 1.

/* K6: the identical call already ran in this conversation, so it
   was authorized then — including its confirmation. A call the
   policy blocked leaves no ToolResult, so a denial cannot approve
   its own retry. */
.decl RetryOfExecutedCall(idx: unsigned)
RetryOfExecutedCall(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    a = $CallTool(fn, args),
    CurrentDepends(mid),
    ToolResult(mid, fn, args).

// @deny_message: Booking-database changes need the user's explicit confirmation first. The most recent user message does not contain one.
// @suggestion: List the exact action details (reservation, flights, cabin, bags, passengers, price and payment method) back to the user and ask them to confirm with "yes" before calling this tool again.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    a = $CallTool(fn, _),
    BookingDbWriteTool(fn),
    !UserConfirmedLatestTurn(),
    !RetryOfExecutedCall(idx).

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   C5-C8: BOOKING AND PAYMENT CONSTRAINTS
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* C5: the agent must obtain the user id from the user first; a
   profile lookup for exactly that id is the checkable evidence. */
// @deny_message: The user id has not been obtained and verified before booking.
// @suggestion: Ask the user for their user id and call get_user_details with it before booking.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    uid = @json_get_str(args, "user_id"),
    !UserProfile(uid, _).

/* C6: at most five passengers per reservation. */
// @deny_message: A reservation may carry at most five passengers.
// @suggestion: Split the party across separate reservations of at most five passengers each.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @json_len(args, "passengers"),
    n > 5.

/* C7: at most one travel certificate, one credit card, three gift
   cards. */
// @deny_message: A reservation may use at most one travel certificate.
// @suggestion: Pay with a single travel certificate plus, if needed, one credit card and up to three gift cards.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @count_payment_prefix(args, "certificate"),
    n > 1.

// @deny_message: A reservation may use at most one credit card.
// @suggestion: Put the balance on a single credit card, or split it across gift cards and a travel certificate.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @count_payment_prefix(args, "credit_card"),
    n > 1.

// @deny_message: A reservation may use at most three gift cards.
// @suggestion: Use at most three gift cards and cover the rest with one credit card or travel certificate.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @count_payment_prefix(args, "gift_card"),
    n > 3.

/* C8: payment methods must already be in the user's profile. The
   rule only fires when a profile for that user is in the chain, and
   only when EVERY profile in the chain is missing the method — so a
   payment the user added mid-conversation is not blocked by an
   older copy of their profile. */
.decl PaymentInSomeProfile(idx: unsigned)
PaymentInSomeProfile(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    a = $CallTool(fn, args),
    PaymentBearingTool(fn),
    ActionUser(idx, uid),
    UserProfile(uid, body),
    @payment_missing_from_profile(args, body) = 0.

// @deny_message: The payment method used is not saved in the user's profile.
// @suggestion: Ask the user to add the payment method to their profile, then re-read the profile with get_user_details and retry with a saved payment id.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    a = $CallTool(fn, _),
    PaymentBearingTool(fn),
    ActionUser(idx, uid),
    UserProfile(uid, _),
    !PaymentInSomeProfile(idx).

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   C9: CONFIRM THE RESERVATION BEFORE WRITING TO IT
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

// @deny_message: This reservation's details have not been retrieved, so the rules that apply to it cannot have been checked.
// @suggestion: Call get_reservation_details for this reservation id first, confirm the facts with the user, then retry.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    ActionRes(idx, rid),
    !ReservationLookedUp(rid).

// @deny_message: This call names no reservation id.
// @suggestion: Obtain the reservation id from the user (or locate it with get_user_details) and include it in the call.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    a = $CallTool(fn, args),
    ReservationWriteTool(fn),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    rid = "".

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   C10-C16: MODIFYING A RESERVATION
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* A reservation counts as basic economy only while no payload in
   the chain shows it in another cabin — an upgrade earlier in the
   conversation lifts the restriction. */
.decl ResSeenNonBasic(rid: symbol)
ResSeenNonBasic(rid) :-
    ResCabin(rid, cabin),
    cabin != "basic_economy".

.decl BasicEconomyRes(rid: symbol)
BasicEconomyRes(rid) :-
    ResCabin(rid, "basic_economy"),
    !ResSeenNonBasic(rid).

/* The proposed flights match a reservation payload we have seen, so
   this call changes only the cabin. */
.decl FlightsUnchanged(idx: unsigned)
FlightsUnchanged(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    ActionRes(idx, rid),
    ReservationPayload(rid, body),
    @flights_same(args, body) = 1.

/* C10: basic economy flights cannot be modified. Changing cabin
   alone is allowed, including out of basic economy. */
// @deny_message: Basic economy flights cannot be modified.
// @suggestion: Keep the existing flights, or change the cabin class first; a basic economy itinerary can only be cancelled, not re-routed.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    ActionRes(idx, rid),
    BasicEconomyRes(rid),
    !FlightsUnchanged(idx).

/* C11: the trip's endpoints must survive the change. Each proposed
   flight number is resolved against the payloads in the chain
   (reservation records and search results); if any leg cannot be
   resolved the rule stays silent rather than guessing. */
.decl NewLegIndex(i: unsigned)
NewLegIndex(0).
NewLegIndex(1).
NewLegIndex(2).
NewLegIndex(3).
NewLegIndex(4).
NewLegIndex(5).

.decl NewLeg(idx: unsigned, fnum: symbol)
NewLeg(idx, fnum) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    NewLegIndex(i),
    fnum = @json_array_get_field_str(args, "flights", i, "flight_number"),
    fnum != "".

.decl NewLegResolved(idx: unsigned, fnum: symbol)
NewLegResolved(idx, fnum) :-
    NewLeg(idx, fnum),
    ChainPayload(body),
    @flight_known(body, fnum) = 1.

.decl NewLegUnresolved(idx: unsigned)
NewLegUnresolved(idx) :-
    NewLeg(idx, fnum),
    !NewLegResolved(idx, fnum).

.decl NewItineraryServes(idx: unsigned, airport: symbol)
NewItineraryServes(idx, ap) :-
    NewLeg(idx, fnum),
    ActionRes(idx, rid),
    ResEndpoint(rid, ap),
    ChainPayload(body),
    @flight_serves(body, fnum, ap) = 1.

// @deny_message: A reservation may be modified without changing its origin, destination or trip type, and the proposed flights no longer serve one of them.
// @suggestion: Keep the same origin and destination. If the user needs a different route, the existing reservation has to be cancelled (if it is eligible) and a new one booked.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    ActionRes(idx, rid),
    ResEndpoint(rid, ap),
    NewLeg(idx, _),
    !NewLegUnresolved(idx),
    !NewItineraryServes(idx, ap).

// @deny_message: This flight change names no flights, which would leave the reservation with no itinerary.
// @suggestion: Include every flight the reservation should end up with — the kept segments as well as the new ones.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    !NewLeg(idx, _).

/* C12: a cabin change is only possible while nothing has flown. */
.decl ResHasFlownSegment(rid: symbol)
ResHasFlownSegment(rid) :-
    ReservationPayload(rid, body),
    @any_flight_flown(body, "2024-05-15") = 1.

/* The call asks for a cabin the reservation is not already in. */
.decl CabinChanged(idx: unsigned)
CabinChanged(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    ActionRes(idx, rid),
    newcabin = @json_get_str(args, "cabin"),
    newcabin != "",
    ResCabin(rid, oldcabin),
    oldcabin != newcabin,
    !ResCabin(rid, newcabin).

// @deny_message: The cabin cannot be changed once any flight in the reservation has been flown.
// @suggestion: Keep the current cabin class. If the user needs something else for the remaining flights, transfer them to a human agent.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    CabinChanged(idx),
    ActionRes(idx, rid),
    ResHasFlownSegment(rid).

/* C13: bags may be added, never removed, and the user is never
   charged for more bags than the reservation carries. */
// @deny_message: Checked bags can be added to a reservation but not removed.
// @suggestion: Call update_reservation_baggages with a total that is at least the reservation's current checked-bag count.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_baggages"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    ActionRes(idx, rid),
    newtotal = @json_get_int(args, "total_baggages"),
    ResBags(rid, current),
    newtotal < current.

// @deny_message: More bags are being charged for than the reservation carries.
// @suggestion: Set nonfree_baggages to the number of bags beyond the user's free allowance, which can never exceed total_baggages.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    a = $CallTool(fn, args),
    BaggageBearingTool(fn),
    nonfree = @json_get_int(args, "nonfree_baggages"),
    total = @json_get_int(args, "total_baggages"),
    nonfree > total.

/* C27: bags the user never asked for are not added. The check is on
   the whole conversation, not just the latest turn, so a request
   made earlier still counts when the agent gets round to it. */
.decl UserMentionedBags()
UserMentionedBags() :-
    UserTurn(mid),
    SentMessage(mid, msg),
    @user_mentions_bags(msg.contents) = 1.

// @deny_message: The user has not asked for checked bags, and bags that are not needed must not be added.
// @suggestion: Ask the user how many checked bags they want before setting a bag count.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    a = $CallTool(fn, args),
    BaggageBearingTool(fn),
    total = @json_get_int(args, "total_baggages"),
    total > 0,
    !UserMentionedBags().

/* C14: the number of passengers is fixed — not even a human agent
   may change it. The rule fires only when no reservation payload
   in the chain agrees with the proposed count. */
.decl PassengerCountMatches(idx: unsigned)
PassengerCountMatches(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_passengers"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    ActionRes(idx, rid),
    n = @json_len(args, "passengers"),
    ResPassengerCount(rid, n).

// @deny_message: The number of passengers on a reservation cannot be changed.
// @suggestion: Submit exactly as many passengers as the reservation already has; to travel with a different party size, cancel (if eligible) and book again.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_passengers"),
    ActionRes(idx, rid),
    ResPassengerCount(rid, _),
    !PassengerCountMatches(idx).

/* C15: passenger details may be corrected, but the travellers
   themselves may not be swapped out. */
.decl PassengerOverlap(idx: unsigned)
PassengerOverlap(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_passengers"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    ActionRes(idx, rid),
    ReservationPayload(rid, body),
    @passengers_substituted(args, body) = 0.

// @deny_message: This replaces the travellers on the reservation rather than correcting their details; a ticket cannot be transferred to a different person.
// @suggestion: Correct the existing passengers' names or dates of birth. If someone else needs to travel, cancel the reservation (if it is eligible) and book a new one for them.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_passengers"),
    ActionRes(idx, rid),
    ReservationPayload(rid, _),
    !PassengerOverlap(idx).

/* C16: flight changes take one gift card or credit card. The API
   accepts a single payment_id, so "single" is structural; what the
   policy has to check is the kind. A travel certificate is excluded
   because its remaining value is not refundable. */
.decl AllowedChangePayment(pid: symbol)
AllowedChangePayment(pid) :-
    Actions(_, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    pid = @json_get_str(args, "payment_id"),
    @str_starts_with(pid, "gift_card") = 1.
AllowedChangePayment(pid) :-
    Actions(_, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    pid = @json_get_str(args, "payment_id"),
    @str_starts_with(pid, "credit_card") = 1.

// @deny_message: A flight change must be paid for or refunded with a single gift card or credit card.
// @suggestion: Ask the user for a gift card or credit card that is already saved in their profile and retry with that payment id.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    pid = @json_get_str(args, "payment_id"),
    pid != "",
    !AllowedChangePayment(pid).

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   C17-C20: CANCELLING A RESERVATION
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

/* C17: the user's identity is established either by a profile
   lookup for the reservation's owner, or by the user stating that
   id in their own turn. */
.decl UserIdentityEstablished(uid: symbol)
UserIdentityEstablished(uid) :-
    UserProfile(uid, _).
UserIdentityEstablished(uid) :-
    ResUser(_, uid),
    UserTurn(mid),
    SentMessage(mid, msg),
    @str_contains(msg.contents, uid) = 1.

// @deny_message: The user id behind this reservation has not been established, so the reservation cannot be confirmed as theirs.
// @suggestion: Ask the user for their user id and call get_user_details with it before cancelling.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "cancel_reservation"),
    ActionRes(idx, rid),
    ResUser(rid, uid),
    !UserIdentityEstablished(uid).

/* C18: the agent must obtain the reason for cancellation. */
.decl CancelReasonStated()
CancelReasonStated() :-
    UserTurn(mid),
    SentMessage(mid, msg),
    @user_states_cancel_reason(msg.contents) = 1.

// @deny_message: The user has not given a reason for cancelling.
// @suggestion: Ask the user why they are cancelling — change of plan, the airline cancelled the flight, or another reason — and note it before calling this tool.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "cancel_reservation"),
    !CancelReasonStated().

/* C19: nothing may be cancelled once part of the trip has flown. */
// @deny_message: Part of this trip has already been flown, so it cannot be cancelled here.
// @suggestion: Transfer the user to a human agent with transfer_to_human_agents, then tell them they are being transferred.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "cancel_reservation"),
    ActionRes(idx, rid),
    ResHasFlownSegment(rid).

/* C20: one of the four grounds for cancellation must hold. The API
   does not check them, so the policy does. */
.decl CoveredReasonStated()
CoveredReasonStated() :-
    UserTurn(mid),
    SentMessage(mid, msg),
    @covered_cancel_reason(msg.contents) = 1.

.decl AirlineCancelledFlight(rid: symbol)
AirlineCancelledFlight(rid) :-
    ReservationPayload(rid, body),
    @res_flight_status_present(body, "cancelled") = 1.
AirlineCancelledFlight(rid) :-
    CurrentDepends(mid),
    ToolResult(mid, "get_flight_status", targs),
    SentMessage(mid, msg),
    status = @str_to_lower(msg.contents),
    @str_contains(status, "cancelled") = 1,
    fnum = @json_get_str(targs, "flight_number"),
    ReservationPayload(rid, body),
    @flight_known(body, fnum) = 1.

.decl CancellationAllowed(rid: symbol)
/* Booked within the last 24 hours. @hours_between returns the
   absolute gap, and -1 when a timestamp will not parse — the
   hours >= 0 guard drops that sentinel so an unreadable created_at
   never reads as "booked moments ago". */
CancellationAllowed(rid) :-
    ResCreated(rid, ts),
    hours = @hours_between(ts, "2024-05-15 15:00:00"),
    hours >= 0,
    hours <= 24.
/* the airline cancelled a flight on it */
CancellationAllowed(rid) :-
    AirlineCancelledFlight(rid).
/* it is a business-class reservation */
CancellationAllowed(rid) :-
    ResCabin(rid, "business").
/* travel insurance plus a covered reason */
CancellationAllowed(rid) :-
    ResInsurance(rid, "yes"),
    CoveredReasonStated().

// @deny_message: This reservation does not meet any of the conditions for cancellation: booked within the last 24 hours, a flight cancelled by the airline, a business-class cabin, or travel insurance with a covered reason.
// @suggestion: Check the reservation's creation time, cabin, insurance and flight status with the user. If none of the conditions hold, explain that and offer transfer_to_human_agents.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "cancel_reservation"),
    ActionRes(idx, rid),
    !CancellationAllowed(rid).

/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   C21-C25: REFUNDS AND COMPENSATION
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

.decl CertUser(idx: unsigned, uid: symbol)
CertUser(idx, uid) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    uid = @json_get_str(args, "user_id"),
    uid != "".

/* C21: compensation is never offered proactively. */
.decl CompensationRequested()
CompensationRequested() :-
    UserTurn(mid),
    SentMessage(mid, msg),
    @user_requests_compensation(msg.contents) = 1.

// @deny_message: Compensation may not be offered unless the user asks for it.
// @suggestion: Do not raise compensation. If the user asks for it, verify their membership level and the disruption first, then issue the certificate.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    !CompensationRequested().

/* C22: regular members are never eligible, whatever they claim. */
// @deny_message: Regular members are not eligible for compensation under any circumstances.
// @suggestion: Tell the user that compensation is limited to silver and gold members. Do not act on a claimed membership level — get_user_details is what counts.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    CertUser(idx, uid),
    MembershipOf(uid, "regular").

/* C23: membership must be verified before anything is offered. */
// @deny_message: The user's membership level has not been verified.
// @suggestion: Call get_user_details for this user id and confirm they are a silver or gold member before issuing a certificate.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    CertUser(idx, uid),
    !MembershipOf(uid, _).

// @deny_message: This certificate names no user.
// @suggestion: Include the user id whose membership was verified with get_user_details.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    uid = @json_get_str(args, "user_id"),
    uid = "".

/* C24/C25: the facts have to be confirmed, and the amount follows
   from them — $100 per passenger for a cancelled flight, $50 per
   passenger for a confirmed delay. */
.decl DelayedFlight(rid: symbol)
DelayedFlight(rid) :-
    ReservationPayload(rid, body),
    @res_flight_status_present(body, "delayed") = 1.
DelayedFlight(rid) :-
    CurrentDepends(mid),
    ToolResult(mid, "get_flight_status", targs),
    SentMessage(mid, msg),
    status = @str_to_lower(msg.contents),
    @str_contains(status, "delayed") = 1,
    fnum = @json_get_str(targs, "flight_number"),
    ReservationPayload(rid, body),
    @flight_known(body, fnum) = 1.

/* A disruption confirmed on a reservation that belongs to the user
   being compensated. */
.decl DisruptionConfirmed(idx: unsigned)
DisruptionConfirmed(idx) :-
    CertUser(idx, uid),
    ResUser(rid, uid),
    AirlineCancelledFlight(rid).
DisruptionConfirmed(idx) :-
    CertUser(idx, uid),
    ResUser(rid, uid),
    DelayedFlight(rid).

// @deny_message: No cancelled or delayed flight has been confirmed on a reservation belonging to this user.
// @suggestion: Look up the user's reservation with get_reservation_details and the flight with get_flight_status, and only offer compensation once the disruption is confirmed.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    !DisruptionConfirmed(idx).

/* The amounts the confirmed facts justify. */
.decl AllowedCertAmount(idx: unsigned, amount: number)
AllowedCertAmount(idx, amount) :-
    CertUser(idx, uid),
    ResUser(rid, uid),
    AirlineCancelledFlight(rid),
    ResPassengerCount(rid, n),
    amount = 100 * n.
AllowedCertAmount(idx, amount) :-
    CertUser(idx, uid),
    ResUser(rid, uid),
    DelayedFlight(rid),
    ResPassengerCount(rid, n),
    amount = 50 * n.

// @deny_message: The certificate amount does not match the policy: $100 per passenger for a cancelled flight, $50 per passenger for a confirmed delay.
// @suggestion: Count the passengers on the affected reservation and send exactly $100 (cancelled) or $50 (delayed) per passenger.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    amount = @json_get_int(args, "amount"),
    DisruptionConfirmed(idx),
    !AllowedCertAmount(idx, amount).
